{'symbol': 'SPGI', 'date': '2021-05-17 09:47:00', 'title': 'S&P Dow Jones Indices Reaches Settlement With SEC', 'text': 'NEW YORK, MAY 17, 2021 /PRNEWSWIRE/ --\xa0S&P DOW JONES INDICES ("S&P DJI"), A DIVISION OF S&P GLOBAL (NYSE: SPGI), ANNOUNCED TODAY THAT IT HAS REACHED A SETTLEMENT WITH THE U.S. SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION ("SEC") TO RESOLVE A MATTER THAT WAS THE SUBJECT OF A PREVIOUSLY DISCLOSED WELLS NOTICE. THE SETTLEMENT ORDER FINDS THAT S&P DJI, WHICH NEITHER ADMITS NOR DENIES THE SEC\'S ALLEGATIONS, ACTED NEGLIGENTLY IN VIOLATION OF SECTION 17(A)(3) OF THE SECURITIES ACT OF 1933 WITH RESPECT TO THE OPERATION OF A THEN UNDISCLOSED QUALITY ASSURANCE MECHANISM AND ITS IMPACT ON CERTAIN REAL-TIME VALUES OF THE S&P 500 VIX SHORT-TERM FUTURES INDEX ER ON A SINGLE BUSINESS DAY, FEBRUARY 5, 2018.'}
